# No Code Comments (hard ban)

## Absolute rule

**Zero comments in application/test/script source.** Do not add them. When you **touch** a source file, **delete every comment in that entire file** in the same change.

Narrating, “why”, history, TODO-in-comment, section banners, Arrange/Act/Assert labels, and restating names are all forbidden. Intent goes into **names, types, and structure** — not prose above the code.

## What is a comment (strip all of these)

- `// ...`
- `/* ... */` and `/** ... */` (JSDoc/TSDoc)
- `{/* ... */}` and `<!-- ... -->`
- C# `///` XML docs (`<summary>`, `<param>`, `<remarks>`, …) on types/members you own
- `#region` / `#endregion` used only as comment banners
- Test ritual labels: `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert`

## Scope

**In scope:** any edited `**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mjs,cjs,cs,cpp,h,hpp,css,scss}` and similar sources under the product trees.

**Out of scope (do not strip):**

- `.md` documentation
- `.mdc` rules, skills, agent prompts
- Tooling that **requires** a directive to work: `// <auto-generated />`, `/// <reference types="..." />`, `// @ts-check`, `#pragma`, license text **only** when the license legally requires retaining it

## Required agent behavior

1. **Never write** a new comment unless the user **explicitly** asked for a comment in that file in the **current** message.
2. **On every edit** of a source file: full-file comment purge (not only your hunk). Leaving old comments “because they were useful” is a rule violation.
3. Do **not** “improve” code by adding clarifying comments; rename symbols or extract functions instead.
4. Do **not** keep `<summary>` / JSDoc on public APIs “for IntelliSense” — names and signatures are enough.
5. Workers/subagents inherit this rule; soft wording like “comment when non-obvious” is **void** here.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
/** Account created; query may already be stripped. */
const [accountCreated, setAccountCreated] = useState(false);

// ✅ GOOD
const [accountCreated, setAccountCreated] = useState(false);
```

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
/// <summary>Canonical OAuth callback URI.</summary>
public static class OAuthRedirectUri { }

// ✅ GOOD
public static class OAuthRedirectUri { }
```

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
// Arrange
var request = BuildRequest();
// Act
var result = await Sut.CreateAsync(request);
// Assert
Assert.NotNull(result);

// ✅ GOOD
var request = BuildRequest();

var result = await Sut.CreateAsync(request);

Assert.NotNull(result);
```

## Sole exception

Keep or add a comment **only** if the user explicitly requests a comment in that file in the current message. No other exceptions.
